Let P, n, d ∈ ℕ and let U ⊆ ℝ^P be open; the subtype ↥U carries the subspace topology and σ-algebra. Write |α| := covectorEuclideanNorm α. Let c : Λⁿ(ℝ^P) → ℝ^d (Covector (Euclid P) n ≃L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) be a continuous linear equivalence with |α| = ‖c(α)‖ for every n-covector α. Let μ₀ be a measure on ↥U and ν : ↥U → ℝ^d a measurable map that is μ₀-integrable on every compact subset of ↥U. Then there are a measure μ on ℝ^P and maps ξ : ℝ^P → Λ_n (MultiVector P n) and β : ℝ^P → Λⁿ (Covector (Euclid P) n) such that:
(a) μ(ℝ^P ∖ U) = 0;
(b) μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U;
(c) ξ is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
(d) |ξ(x)(α)| ≤ |α| for every x and every n-covector α;
(e) β is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
(f) there is C ∈ ℝ with ‖β(x)‖ ≤ C for every x, in the operator norm of Λⁿ;
(g) |β(x)| ≤ 1 for every x;
(h) ξ(x)(β(x)) = 1 for μ-a.e. x;
(i) for every map ω : ℝ^P → Λⁿ (DifferentialForm (Euclid P) n), ∫_{↥U} ⟨c(ω(x)), ν(x)⟩ dμ₀(x) = ∫ ξ(y)(ω(y)) dμ(y), as Bochner integrals.

Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P, T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) (GeometricCurrentOn U n), μ a measure on ℝ^P, ξ : ℝ^P → Λ_n (MultiVector P n) and β : ℝ^P → Λⁿ (Covector (Euclid P) n). Write |α| := covectorEuclideanNorm α. Assume:
(i) μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U;
(ii) ξ is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
(iii) |ξ(x)(α)| ≤ |α| for every x and α;
(iv) T(ω) = ∫ ξ(x)(ω(x)) dμ(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U);
(v) β is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
(vi) there is C ∈ ℝ with ‖β(x)‖ ≤ C for every x (operator norm);
(vii) |β(x)| ≤ 1 for every x;
(viii) ξ(x)(β(x)) = 1 for μ-a.e. x.
Then μ(W') ≤ M_W(T) = T.massOn W for all W, W' ⊆ ℝ^P such that W' is open, W' ⊂⊂ U (CompactlyContained W' U: closure W' is compact and contained in U) and W' ⊆ W.
